# The operators the browser's runtime is built with.
#
# Kept by hand rather than generated from one model, so that widening it and
# shipping the network that needs the wider set can happen in either order.
# The build workflow checks every model in web/public against this line and
# refuses one that asks for more.
#
# The first fifteen are what the distilled student needs. ReduceMax and
# Sigmoid were added on 10 September 2026 for channel attention, which our
# full network has and the student was built without.
# The float kernels were added on 16 September 2026. The page had been playing
# our own half of the fused network alone -- the half the joined head weighs
# about 0.02 against Mortal's 1.00 -- because a fused checkpoint carries that
# half under `model` and the exporter read it. The whole fusion is exported
# now, and it is exported in float: eight bits cost its value head more than
# a tenth of that head's own spread. Convolution, matrix products, Mortal's
# batch normalisation and the pieces of its head are what the fusion adds,
# with the comparisons its legality mask goes through. The quantised kernels
# stay until nothing shipped needs them.
ai.onnx;17;Add,BatchNormalization,Cast,Concat,Constant,ConstantOfShape,Conv,ConvInteger,Div,DynamicQuantizeLinear,Equal,Expand,Flatten,Gather,Gemm,Greater,InstanceNormalization,MatMul,MatMulInteger,Mul,Not,ReduceMax,ReduceMean,ReduceSum,Relu,Reshape,Shape,Sigmoid,Softplus,Split,Squeeze,Sub,Tanh,Unsqueeze,Where
